  "answer": "The Enterprise onboarding target range in the playbook is 8–10 weeks [NL-005-S02][NL-031-S02], and the observed Enterprise average/median is 8.7 weeks [NL-012-S06][NL-031-S02][NL-031-S03]. So the observed duration is within the playbook range, near the lower-middle.\n\nEnterprise onboarding is longer than simpler plans because Starter and Growth customers typically upload clean, public-facing documents and require little or no complex permission mapping [NL-012-S06][NL-031-S02], whereas Enterprise customers need security reviews, custom data-retention configurations, SSO setups, and OCR processing for scanned PDF policies [NL-012-S06][NL-031-S02]. Enterprise implementations also add custom SSO/directory integrations, advanced OCR queues, DPA validation, BYOK, and extended UAT [NL-005-S09]. The main delay drivers are permission mapping (45% of delays), source ingestion cleanup (30%), and OCR processing (25%) [NL-012-S06].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
